       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The risk is higher because amlodipine has a long half-life of about 30 to 50 hours. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make this dose safe.\n\nYou've also said you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber or be verified by one.\n\n- **If 5 mg or 10 mg was intended**, confirm the dose and I'll enter it. Usual starting doses are 2.5 to 5 mg once daily, up to 10 mg.\n- **If 50 mg is deliberate**, which would be highly unusual, the prescriber should contact pharmacy and enter it directly with documented justification.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
