       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. A 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine could seriously harm the patient, and the confirmation didn't come from a prescriber with a clinical reason for it.\n\nThese options would work:\n\n- **A prescriber enters or co-signs the order.** They can document why the dose is needed, and pharmacy can review it.\n- **I enter a standard dose.** Give me a prescriber's intended dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **A pharmacist or the medicine service attending reviews it.** This is the best route if you're not sure what the patient needs.\n\nIf the patient has already received a dose like this, tell the clinical team now so they can monitor blood pressure and heart rate."
